# CLI Documentation Closure — Gaps Index

Open questions and deliberate exclusions surfaced by the initial `beaver-cli` audit
(2026-09-17) that this roadmap depends on resolving, or has already decided not to resolve.
Same role as `beaver-desktop/features/*/gaps/00-index.docs`: the backlog to work from when a
version's status note says "verify," "classify," or "needs a live smoke-test."

Two kinds of entry:
- **Blocking** — a version cannot be completed as specified until this is resolved.
- **Deferred / decision-needed** — doesn't block the roadmap, but needs an explicit answer
  before the affected page(s) publish.

---

## 001 — `container` vs. `containers` naming — **DECISION-NEEDED (Era 5 V16)**

`beaver-cli/commands/container/container.go` registers both `Use: "container <name> <action>
[args]"` and `Use: "containers"` as apparently distinct commands, and this repo has separate
`container.mdx` and `containers.mdx` pages already. Not yet confirmed whether both are live,
top-level, user-facing commands or whether one is legacy.

**Consequence:** Era 5 V16 must confirm both are real before treating the existing two-page
split as correct; if one is stale, it needs to be merged/redirected rather than left as an
apparently-duplicate pair.

---

## 002 — `observe` vs. `observability` overlap — **DECISION-NEEDED (Era 8 V27–V28)**

`observe/observe.go` registers a standalone `Use: "observe [service]"` command, separate
from the `observability` group (`logs`/`metrics`/`traffic`/`latency`/`active`/`live`). Not
yet confirmed whether these overlap in function or are cleanly distinct (e.g. `observe`
might be a single-pane summary while `observability` subcommands are the individual views).

**Consequence:** Era 8 V27's family-shape decision and V28's `observe` verification must
state the relationship explicitly. If they overlap significantly, the docs need to say so
rather than presenting two commands that appear to do the same thing with no explanation.

---

## 003 — `plan`/`plans` staleness — **DECISION-NEEDED (Era 12 V42)**

`cli/plan.mdx` and `cli/plans.mdx` exist with no matching `beaver-cli/commands/` directory.
Per `CLAUDE.md`'s note on the prior product model ("Build Once. Deploy Anywhere." replacing
an earlier hosting-plan-centric model), these are the strongest candidates in the whole
audit for pages describing a **removed** command from before the repositioning, rather than
a naming mismatch with something that still exists.

**Consequence:** Era 1 V2 must confirm via source (not inference from `CLAUDE.md` alone)
whether any current command produces "plan" semantics (e.g. `service database` or `billing`
subcommands might use the word incidentally). If nothing current matches, both pages are
removed (with a redirect if there's meaningful inbound-link risk) in Era 12 V42, per
`CLAUDE.md`'s general instruction not to reintroduce the prior model — but the removal
itself, not just the staleness, must be an explicit, logged decision.

---

## 004 — `internal` command group publication status — **RESOLVED (Era 1 V2, 2026-09-17)**

`beaver-cli/commands/internal/` (9 files) was the strongest naming signal in the audit that
this group might not belong in public docs. Era 1's extraction settled it definitively
rather than leaving it a judgment call: **`internal/` contains zero `cobra.Command`
definitions anywhere** (confirmed by direct grep for `cobra.Command` across every file in
the directory) — it is a support/library package, not a command group at all. The same is
true of `deployui`, `envbanner`, `projectconfig`, `projectcontext`, `state`, and `ui` (43
files total across all seven).

**Resolution:** all seven directories are excluded from the command inventory entirely —
not as an `excluded` classification decision (Era 10's original plan), but because there is
no command to classify. Era 10 V34's classification work now applies only to `admin` and
`mcpcmd`, whose `Hidden: true` commands are real commands with a real visibility question.
See `inventory/00-summary.docs`, "Excluded directories" table.

---

## 005 — `mcpcmd` public-vs-internal transport question — **DECISION-NEEDED (Era 11 V39)**

Unclear from the group name alone whether `mcpcmd` (2 files) exposes a user-facing MCP
integration (connecting external MCP clients/servers to `beaver` — legitimately
documentable) or internal MCP transport plumbing used by the platform's own AI features
(not documentable, per Invariant 6 and the same logic as gap 004).

**Consequence:** Era 11 V39 must resolve this from source before drafting; the two possible
answers lead to very different pages (a full integration guide vs. an exclusion entry).

**Resolution (Era 11 V39, 2026-09-17):** `mcpcmd`'s only command is `mcp-serve`
(`commands/mcpcmd/mcpcmd.go`), and it is internal transport plumbing, not a user-facing
integration. Confirmed directly from source: `Hidden: true`, and its own doc comment states
"a user never types this... an integration point for the harness config `harness/claude.go`
and `harness/codexserver.go` generate" — it's spawned by an AI coding harness (Claude Code,
Codex) as a child process over stdio, not something a `beaver` user runs. **Determination:
excluded**, no page written. This is the same shape as gap 004's exclusions, just found via
a real (but hidden) command rather than an empty directory.

---

## 006 — `config schema` disclosure risk — **BLOCKING (Era 9 V31)**

`config schema` is a plausible name for a command that either (a) prints a JSON Schema used
to validate a user's own config file (safe, genuinely useful to document — helps users write
valid config, IDE autocomplete, etc.) or (b) surfaces something closer to the internal
deployment-contract schema `CLAUDE.md` explicitly protects. The audit could not distinguish
these from the command name and file count alone.

**Consequence:** Era 9 V31 cannot write this subcommand's section until the actual output is
checked against source. This is the single most consequential disclosure determination in
the roadmap — a wrong call here is the exact scenario `docs.txt` opened by worrying about.

---

## 007 — Live-verification gaps (multiple commands) — **DEFERRED (Era 13 V44)**

Several commands' consequences can plausibly be inferred from source but would be better
confirmed by actually running them: `service cluster upgrade`/`replace-member` (does the
cluster stay available during the operation?), `promote` (does it rebuild or reuse an
existing artifact?), `status`'s exact output fields. None of these block their family era's
initial draft (source review is sufficient per Invariant 1 to write a reasonable first
pass), but all are flagged for Era 13 V44's live-verification pass rather than shipping as
permanently "reviewed against source only" if a live check is feasible by then.

**Consequence:** Not blocking. These pages ship from Eras 4/5/7/8 marked "reviewed against
source"; V44 upgrades the marking to "verified" for whichever of these a live run confirms.

---

## 008 — No automated inventory-refresh tooling in V1 — **DEFERRED (post-roadmap, noted in Era 13 V47)**

The Era 1 extraction (grep-based `Use:`/flag-site census) is manual and was run once during
scoping. Era 13 V47 establishes a *periodic manual* re-run cadence, not automation.

**Consequence:** Not blocking for this roadmap's V1. If the manual cadence proves to lag
(discovered via the Era 13 V46 per-change gate catching drift the periodic refresh should
have caught first), a small script formalizing the extraction becomes the natural follow-up
— out of scope here, recorded so it's a decision to defer, not an oversight.

---

## 009 — `output.RegisterFlags()` shared flags invisible to `commands.csv` — **RESOLVED (Era 2 V7, 2026-09-17; count corrected 2026-09-17)**

Found while building the shared-flags page: `--json`/`--output`/`--quiet`/`--yes`/`--wait`/
`--timeout` are attached to a large set of commands via one shared call,
`output.RegisterFlags(cmd)` (defined in `beaver-cli/output/output.go`, outside `commands/`).
`extract_commands.py`'s literal `Flags().Kind("name", ...)` pattern doesn't match this
indirect call, so `commands.csv` under-reports these commands' flag counts by 6 each.

**Resolution:** not fixed in the extractor (a deliberate scope decision — see
`inventory/00-summary.docs`'s note on this gap for why re-deriving statistically would be
worse than the direct source read already in hand). `cli/shared-flags.mdx` documents all six
flags authoritatively from `output.go` directly, including `--wait`'s actual poll/timeout
behavior (`output.Wait`: polls periodically until done, context-cancelled, or timeout;
timeout does not cancel the underlying operation, only the CLI's wait).

**Count correction (Phase 1 re-verification, 2026-09-17):** the original "69 commands"
figure was a hand-estimate and was stale — a raw `grep -c output.RegisterFlags` gives 145
call sites, but call sites and affected commands aren't 1:1 (some call sites are one command,
some are a `for _, c := range []*cobra.Command{...}` loop covering 20+ commands in one call).
`build_summary.py` now computes the real distinct-command count live from source every
regeneration (`count_register_flags_commands()`) instead of hardcoding a number — currently
**196 commands**. Re-running `build_summary.py` after any `beaver-cli` change keeps this
figure current automatically; no more manual re-counting.

**Consequence for Phase 2:** every family era should check whether its group's commands call
`output.RegisterFlags` (`grep -rn output.RegisterFlags commands/<group>/`) before assuming a
command has no `--wait`/`--json`/etc. just because it's absent from `commands.csv`.

---

## 010 — Era 10 V34 classification results — **RESOLVED (Era 10 V34–V36, 2026-09-17)**

Per-command classification, source-verified (all three `admin` commands confirmed
`Hidden: true` directly in `commands/admin/*.go`; `mystic`/`preflight`/`initcmd` confirmed
not hidden and registered as ordinary root commands in `main.go`):

- **`admin` (all 3 commands)** — **operator-only-but-mentionable**, not fully excluded.
  Reason to not exclude outright: `commands/connect/connect.go` prints `beaver admin
  connect-edge-node` directly in a user-facing error message when an admin account attempts
  `beaver connect`, so the name is already exposed to end users on a real error path.
  `cli/admin.mdx` published as a minimal page (what it is, who it's for, no flag detail) per
  the lighter template V35 specifies for this classification tier.
- **`mystic`** — **public**. Not hidden; `doctor`/`stats` are genuinely useful end-user
  diagnostics for build performance. Full page written (`cli/mystic.mdx`).
- **`preflight`** — **public**. Full page written (`cli/preflight.mdx`), check-category
  structure mirrors `doctor.mdx` per V35's consistency requirement.
- **`initcmd`** — **public**; existing `cli/init.mdx` already accurate, left as-is.
- **`envbanner`, `internal`** — already resolved **excluded** by gap 004 (zero
  `cobra.Command` definitions — library code, not CLI surface). No further action needed;
  V36's "log the excluded commands" requirement was already satisfied by gap 004's entry.

**Consequence:** Era 10 (V34–V36) closes with zero ambiguous rows for this family — every
command is `documented`, `documented-minimal` (admin), or `excluded-with-a-logged-reason`
(via gap 004).

---

## 011 — Era 1 extractor under-counted commands; fixed (Phase 1 re-verification) — **RESOLVED (2026-09-17)**

Phase 1's own re-verification pass (V1's mandated "spot-check 5 groups against a fresh
manual grep") found and fixed three real extraction bugs in `extract_commands.py`, none of
which were caught by the original scoping run:

1. **Anonymous inline command literals** (`parent.AddCommand(&cobra.Command{Use: "init",
   ...}, &cobra.Command{Use: "sync", ...})` — no var assignment, no factory function) were
   invisible to every existing pass. Found via `commands/config/wizard.go`'s `config init`
   and `config sync` — two real, currently undocumented commands that did not exist
   *anywhere* in the inventory before this fix. New Pass D added to the extractor.
2. **Root-level commands outside `commands/` entirely** — `beaver shell` (`root/root.go`)
   and `beaver destroy <container>` (`main.go`, a destructive short-form alias for
   `container <name> delete`) were never scanned at all, since `CLI_ROOT` only walks
   `commands/`. `beaver destroy` in particular had zero documentation coverage anywhere in
   the repo. Both files now scanned explicitly as a synthetic `root` group, with the
   program's own `beaver` root command filtered back out.
3. **Systematic source-line under-reporting**: `CMD_ASSIGN_RE`'s leading `(?:^|\n)\s*` can
   swallow blank/comment lines before a `var Foo = &cobra.Command{` line, anchoring the
   recorded line number to whatever precedes it instead of the actual line — verified
   concretely on `commands/account/account.go` (recorded line 32, actual line 34). Fixed by
   citing the variable-name capture group's own position instead of the whole match's start.

A full-repo sweep after all three fixes (every `&cobra.Command{` literal in `commands/` +
the two root files, checked against Pass A/B/C/D's coverage) confirms **zero remaining
unaccounted literals** — up from 442→443 confirmed-correct commands with accurate line
numbers, from an inventory that silently dropped 4 real commands and mis-cited most of the
rest by 1+ lines.

Also resolved in the same pass — three more "documented under a different name" mappings
`cross_reference.py` was missing (the pages exist and are correct; only the group↔page
mapping table was incomplete): `reconcilecmd` ↔ `cli/reconcile.mdx`, `skillscmd` ↔
`cli/skills.mdx`, `statecmd` ↔ `cli/state.mdx`, plus `root` ↔ `cli/shell.mdx`. And two pages
that are real and current but aren't a per-group reference page at all —
`cli/shared-flags.mdx` (Era 2 V7's own deliverable) and `cli/containers.mdx` (a second,
legitimate top-level command inside the `container` group directory, not a separate group)
— reclassified out of "orphan" into a new `NOT_A_GROUP_PAGE` exemption list instead of
appearing as unresolved gaps on every future run.

**Remaining real, still-open items after this pass** (not extractor bugs — genuine
documentation gaps for Phase 2 to pick up): `beaver spec` (`speccmd`, visible, compatibility-
promised, zero doc page) and `beaver destroy` (found by fix #2 above, zero doc page, and
destructive — high priority for whichever family era picks it up, most naturally alongside
`container.mdx`/`containers.mdx` since `destroy` is explicitly a short-form alias for
`container <name> delete`). `mcpcmd` stays excluded per gap 005.

**Consequence:** every later era's "my family's rows" filter (V4's stated purpose) is now
reading from a genuinely complete, line-accurate inventory rather than one with silent gaps.

---

## 012 — Phase 2 re-verification: two groups never assigned to any era; several pages stale/thin despite "done" status — **RESOLVED (2026-09-17)**

A full Phase 2 re-verification (per-family flag-coverage cross-check: every `commands.csv`
flag checked for a literal mention on its mapped page, all 54 groups) found real content
gaps despite every Era 3–11 status header reading "✅ done, verified 2026-09-17":

**Planning omissions** — two real command groups were never listed in any Phase 2 era's
family assignment in `00-architecture.docs` at all (not excluded, just never scoped to
anyone): `environment` (9 commands, 7 flags) and `project` (5 commands, 3 flags). A third,
`speccmd` (`beaver spec`), was likewise unassigned. Nothing enforced that the family table's
implicit coverage was exhaustive against the actual 54-group inventory.

**Stale/thin pages carried forward from before this roadmap** — `cli/environment.mdx` and
`cli/project.mdx` were both pre-existing 19-line example-only stubs (no Purpose/Syntax/
Flags/Consequences sections, matching neither the Era 2 V6 template nor this repo's other
family pages) that were never rewritten despite `doc_status.csv` marking both `documented`
— a reminder that "documented" there means "a page with this name exists," per
`cross_reference.py`'s own docstring ("weak signal, still useful triage"), not "complete."
`cli/init.mdx` was the same shape (18 lines, missing `--from-existing`).

**Small real gaps in otherwise-substantial pages**, all source-verified and fixed: `config.mdx`
missing `ConfigCmd`'s six non-interactive seed flags and `bind add`/`volume add`'s flags
entirely; `alie.mdx` missing the `audit` command and three flags; `edge.mdx` missing four
flags across `firewall rule add`/`update`/`ban`; `firewall.mdx` missing one; `container.mdx`
missing `open`'s `--live`.

**Confirmed accurate on re-check, not gaps:** `plan.mdx`/`validate.mdx` (verified word-for-
word against `projectcontract.PlanCmd`/`ValidateCmd` source — both exactly right); `beaver
destroy` (found missing from the *inventory* in the Phase 1 pass, but already correctly
documented on `container.mdx` all along — a tooling gap, not a content gap); `plans.mdx`
(Phase 1's gap 003 flagged this as a stale-page candidate — re-verification found `beaver
plans` is a real, current `billing` subcommand, correctly cross-linked from `billing.mdx`;
gap 003 is now fully closed, not deferred).

**Resolution:** all six pages rewritten or extended (`environment.mdx`, `project.mdx`,
`init.mdx` fully rewritten to template; `config.mdx`/`alie.mdx`/`edge.mdx`/`firewall.mdx`/
`container.mdx` extended with the specific missing content); `cli/spec.mdx` written new and
added to `docs.json`'s Utilities group; `cross_reference.py`'s `MANUAL_GROUP_TO_PAGES`
corrected for `projectcontract` (→ `plan`/`validate`/`config`, not a nonexistent own page),
`container` (→ also `containers`), `billing` (→ also `plans`), and `speccmd` (→ `spec`);
`KNOWN_STALE_PAGES` emptied now that gap 003 is fully resolved rather than deferred. Full
pipeline re-run: **0 orphan pages, 1 correctly-excluded undocumented group (`mcpcmd`)**, down
from the prior run's residual ambiguity. `mint broken-links` clean. Disclosure re-check
(checkpoint-term grep) on every changed page: all hits reviewed, all compliant — no
mechanism language found or introduced.

**Consequence:** a status header of "done, verified" on an era file is a claim about scope
having been *addressed*, not proof every page reached template-complete — this gap exists so
a future session re-reads that distinction rather than trusting the header alone. The
per-family flag-coverage cross-check used to find this (commands.csv flags vs. literal
mentions on the mapped page) is cheap enough to re-run after any future `beaver-cli` change
and is the recommended first step of Era 13's periodic-refresh cadence (gap 008), not just a
one-time audit.

---

## 013 — `admin` public documentation removed entirely — **SUPERSEDES gap 010's `admin` resolution (2026-09-17)**

Explicit user instruction: "remove in the docs all admin sections." `cli/admin.mdx` deleted,
removed from `docs.json`'s Utilities group. This replaces gap 010's earlier
**operator-only-but-mentionable / `documented-minimal`** classification for `admin` with a
stricter one: **not published at all**, full stop — not even the minimal page. The
underlying facts gap 010 found are unchanged and still worth keeping in mind if this is
revisited: all 3 `admin` commands are `Hidden: true` in source, and
`commands/connect/connect.go` prints `beaver admin connect-edge-node` in a user-facing error
message on `beaver connect` (still visible as plain text on `cli/connect.mdx`'s Results &
Failures table — not a link, doesn't break anything, left as-is since it's describing real
error output a user might see, not a doc page).

**Consequence:** `admin` reverts to `doc_status: undocumented` in the regenerated inventory
(`00-summary.docs`), the same bucket `mcpcmd` already sits in for a different reason
(internal transport, gap 005) — both are now "intentionally not public," just via different
paths (mcpcmd: never had a page; admin: had one, removed by instruction). If a future session
re-runs the Era 1 extraction and sees `admin` as "undocumented," this entry is why — it is
not a rediscovered gap to fill, it's a standing decision. Don't re-create `cli/admin.mdx`
without checking this entry first.
